// Baguette Channel Layout — Ui Integration And Acceptance
// ROLE: INTEGRATE - wire owners together; do not reimplement their logic.
//
// Purpose: baguette line within channel or ring segment
// Boundary: this task may only orchestrate; each step below must already be owned
//           and tested by the module named in the record's external_owner_interfaces.
//
// Order: Use document mm and document tolerance; never hard-code arbitrary tolerance as PASS threshold. Gem cut/size metadata and rigid instance transform remain coherent. No naked/invalid BRep when closed geometry is claimed; OCCT validity check if shape is generated. Preview must be ephemeral; Accept is atomic transaction; Undo/Redo reverts exactly. Stable EntityId/GemId/FeatureId/LayerId when mapping is unambiguous; otherwise explicit conflict. Source dependency and style provenance survive save/open without silent detach. No dependencies on specs/90-after and no duplicate M06 settings or M07 cutters. Proposed fixture identifiers; user-independent procedural geometry only; register exact files, SHA, inputs, oracle and tolerances when source/toolchain available. Manual references inherited from canonical L3; if parent_l2_range only, do not present as command-level proof. Reinspect relevant PDF pages before asserting behavior. Expose command through real menu/F6/selection context; use existing command dispatch and semantic state, not dummy buttons. Implement preview/cancel/confirm with no phantom document objects; ensure control values use mm/deg and invalid controls are disabled. Run guided UI scenario: Create a baguette channel row; compare corner and straight sections. Check viewport response, Undo/Redo, save/open and source-edit history with screenshots/log. Mark READY_FOR_MANUAL_TEST only after runtime UI and BE tests; DONE only after human sign-off
//
// Integration checklist:
//   1. resolve owners through the parent service contract, not through UI handles
//   2. keep one transaction boundary: either the whole sequence commits or nothing does
//   3. on any step error, roll back what this sequence already changed and report the failing step
//   4. assert identity survives: same stable IDs before and after, no stale scene reference
//
// Contract under test: input: guide/rail and baguette dimensions; output: baguette layout along specified channel; error_type: Result<T, DomainError> (illustrative Rust convention; must align with checked-out workspace)
// Oracle: UI command registration resolves to real service; disabled state for missing selection/dependency
// Negative oracle: negative channel width, corner self-intersection, collision rejected
